WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.467
Coding Exercise 1 checks whether you can translate a mixed Boolean rule correctly.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:10.512
The two alternatives are age sixty-five or older, OR Kidney Disease.

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:17.152
Those alternatives belong together. Then explicit consent must apply to the entire grouped condition.

00:00:17.152 --> 00:00:23.947
Before writing the SQL, say the rule aloud: the patient must either be at least sixty-five or have Kidney

00:00:23.947 --> 00:00:27.087
Disease, and in either case consent must be explicitly true.

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:32.837
That sentence tells you where the parentheses belong.

00:00:32.837 --> 00:00:37.197
Use the starter query and complete only the required logic.

00:00:37.197 --> 00:00:41.427
Then run the check. If a patient with false consent appears, do not randomly change operators.

00:00:41.427 --> 00:00:43.887
Look specifically at the grouping.

00:00:43.887 --> 00:00:50.567
Ask whether consent is being applied to both alternatives or only one.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:55.947
This exercise is intentionally short because the difficult part is not syntax.

00:00:55.947 --> 00:00:59.120
The difficult part is translating the policy correctly.
